<section class="page-hero container"><span class="eyebrow">A SIMPLE RHYTHM FOR LASTING LEARNING</span><h1>Find your<br><span class="purple-text">learning loop.</span></h1><p>Start with something worth remembering. Give it a little attention, a little practice, and a place to come back to.</p></section>
<section class="section container section-first"><?php require __DIR__ . '/../partials/steps.php'; ?></section>
<section class="section features-section"><div class="container how-detail-grid"><article class="card editorial-card"><span class="feature-icon"><?= icon('lightbulb',25) ?></span><h2>Think first.<br>Then turn the card.</h2><p>Read the question and try to retrieve the answer from memory. Select “Show Answer” when you’re ready, compare your response, and honestly rate how recall felt.</p><p>The answer is sent only after you choose to reveal it. A small pause gives you space to do the thinking.</p></article><article class="card editorial-card"><span class="feature-icon tone-1"><?= icon('loop',25) ?></span><h2>A schedule that<br>grows with you.</h2><p>Again brings a card back in 10 minutes. Successful recalls extend its interval. Hard moves cautiously, Good follows the normal progression, and Easy moves further ahead.</p><p>The scheduler adapts each card individually. This is a practical study aid, not a guarantee of a particular learning outcome.</p></article></div></section>
<section class="section container faq-section"><div class="section-intro"><span class="eyebrow">A FEW HELPFUL DETAILS</span><h2>Before your<br>first card.</h2></div><div class="faq-list"><details><summary>What should I put on a flashcard? <?= icon('plus',18) ?></summary><p>Focus on one idea. Write a clear question on the front and a concise answer on the back. Use the optional explanation for context, examples, or a memory cue.</p></details><details><summary>What is the difference between review and practice? <?= icon('plus',18) ?></summary><p>Review selects cards that are due and updates their schedule from your ratings. Practice includes cards even if they aren’t due; it records the practice activity while leaving review due dates unchanged.</p></details><details><summary>How does my study streak work? <?= icon('plus',18) ?></summary><p>A study day is a UTC calendar day with at least one recorded review or practice rating. Your current streak continues when your latest study day is today or yesterday. Logging in alone does not count.</p></details><details><summary>Can I take my cards with me? <?= icon('plus',18) ?></summary><p>Yes. Open any of your decks and export its questions, answers, and explanations as CSV. You can also import a UTF-8 CSV file into your own deck.</p></details><details><summary>Do I need to install anything? <?= icon('plus',18) ?></summary><p>Learners use BrainLoop in a browser. To run it locally with XAMPP, copy the complete BrainLoop folder into <code>C:\xampp\htdocs\</code>, start Apache and MySQL, and open <code>http://localhost/BrainLoop/</code>. The project README explains database configuration and hosting requirements.</p></details></div></section>
